    },
    {
      "source": "SlowMist",
      "text": "The decentralized algorithmic stablecoin protocol Pythia was attacked due to a vulnerability in its staking contract, resulting in a loss of 21 ETH (approximately $53,000)."
    },
    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "Pythia Finance's staking contract on Ethereum Mainnet was exploited through a reentrancy vulnerability on 2,3 September 2024, resulting in a loss of approximately 21 ETH (~$53,000). The attacker repeatedly claimed staking rewards by triggering reentrancy before the contract updated its internal state. The claimRewards() function in the Pythia Staking contract allowed ERC20 token transfers before updating the user's reward state. This violated the Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern and enabled reentrancy, letting an attacker claim rewards multiple times before the state was reset."
    }
  ],
